    "title": "Red Sox to finish series vs. Tigers in a day-game today. How to watch",
    "text": "April 20, 2026, 7:09 a.m. ETThe Red Sox will finish a four-game series against the Detroit Tigers in a day-game today, April 20.Todays Red Sox vs. Tigers game begins at 11:10 a.m.The Red Sox are 1-2 in the series so far.In the team's current series against the Detroit Tigers at Fenway Park in Boston, the Red Sox are 1-2.But there's time to even the series this morning when the Sox play their fourth, and final game in the series.Today is Patriots Day, so the Boston Marathon will be bringing many people to the city along with the Red Sox game.The Sox have a record of 8-13 going into today's game, so the team could definitely use a win against the Tigers, who have a record of 12-10 and are in second place in the AL Central.The Red Sox are in fourth place in the AL East, with the Toronto Blue Jays sitting in last place.Here's how to watch this morning's game against the Red Sox and the Detroit Tigers.Where is today's Red Sox game?It'll be a home game at Fenway Park in Boston.What time is today's Red Sox game?The first pitch is slated for 11:10 a.m. today, Monday, April 20, 2026.Who is the starting pitcher for the Red Sox today?It'll be right-hand pitcher Sonny Gray, who is 2-1 on the season and has an ERA of 4.43. He has 11 strikeouts on the season.How can people watch today's game against the Tigers?It'll air live on NESN, and will be streaming on FuboTV and MLB.TV.Watch the game on FuboWho do the Red Sox play after they play the Tigers?The Red Sox will play a series against their heated rival, the New York Yankees. That series will be played at home at Fenway Park in Boston, and will begin this Tuesday, April 21. 2026.Our editors independently choose our recommendations. Some content is produced with paid support from a third party, however our editorial decisions remain independent. If you buy through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices and availability may change.",
